  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Isabel, you're verified. I'm sorry about this. Getting meat when you ordered a vegetarian dish is upsetting.\n\nOrder Q-7901 from Saffron Lane was handed to you in person at 6:50 PM. It was for one paneer tikka masala and one jeera rice. The order record doesn't show how the wrong dish ended up in your bag. I can't tell whether the restaurant packed it wrong or something else happened, and I don't want to guess.\n\nI can't issue a refund or credit myself right now. Your account has had several refunds in the last 30 days, and our policy sends any compensation request on an account in that situation to a specialist for review. I've escalated your case (reference ESC-700) with the full details. A specialist will follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise what the outcome will be.\n\nPlease don't eat the dish. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks for escalating it. I should tell you, I already ate a few bites before I realized it was chicken, and I've been sick to my stomach since. I'm feeling better now, but that's a big part of why I'm so upset. I'm also a Forkful Plus member, so I'd expect this to be handled properly. Is there any way someone can look at this sooner than 24 hours?"
  },
  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "escalate_to_human",
   "args": {
    "customer_id": "D209",
    "order_id": "Q-7901",
    "reason": "food_safety",
    "summary": "Customer reports that after receiving chicken tikka masala instead of paneer tikka masala on order Q-7901 (she is vegetarian), she ate a few bites and has felt sick to her stomach since. She says she is feeling better now. Separate fraud_review escalation ESC-700 already exists for the same order. She asked whether it could be looked at sooner than 24 hours."
   },
   "result": {
    "escalation_id": "ESC-701",
    "follow_up": "within 24 hours"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I'm sorry you got sick, Isabel. I'm glad you're feeling better.\n\nI've opened a second escalation (reference ESC-701) for the food-safety side, so a specialist will see that you ate some of the dish and felt ill. Both escalations are on order Q-7901.\n\nI can't speed up the follow-up. The timeframe for both is within 24 hours, and I can't offer anything faster. Plus membership gives you higher limits, but it doesn't change how these reviews work. I also can't promise what the outcome will be.\n\nIf your symptoms get worse, please contact a medical professional. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thank you for opening the second escalation. I understand you can't speed it up, but I'd like it on record that I'm a Plus member and I still expect a refund for something I didn't order. I'm not going to push you on the details today, so I'll wait for the specialist.\n\nThanks for your help. I'll keep an eye out for their follow-up."
  }
